    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Pacific herring, Central Coast\"\nparams:\n  stock_id: \"herring_cc\"\n---\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n::: {.disclaimer}\nExploratory personal project. Not an official assessment and not a seafood recommendation.\n:::\n\n::::: {.columns}\n\n:::: {.column width=\"36%\"}\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"stock-card\">\n<div class=\"card-head\" style=\"background:#2471a3;\">\n<div class=\"card-species\">Pacific herring</div>\n<div class=\"card-title\">Pacific herring, Central Coast</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"badges\">\n<span class=\"badge\" style=\"background:#d98c00;\">DFO 2024: Cautious</span>\n<span class=\"badge tier\">Data tier C</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"stat\">1.97× LRP</div>\n<div class=\"stat-label\">Biomass relative to the limit reference point, 2018</div>\n<img class=\"spark\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"Sparkline of biomass relative to the limit reference point for Pacific herring, Central Coast\"/>\n<dl>\n<dt>Evidence</dt>\n<dd>Biomass and catch trends, no MSY ratios</dd>\n<dt>Managed by</dt>\n<dd>Fisheries and Oceans Canada (DFO)</dd>\n<dt>Status method</dt>\n<dd>Scientific Peer Review Process</dd>\n<dt>RAM assessment period</dt>\n<dd>1949-2018</dd>\n<dt>Biomass estimates</dt>\n<dd>1951 to 2018</dd>\n</dl>\n<div class=\"fun\">Fun fact: Herring spawn in shallow coastal water, laying sticky eggs on kelp and eelgrass.</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n::::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"4%\"}\n::::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](herring_cc_files/figure-html/trend-1.png){width=768}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n[Download the 2-page rapid assessment (PDF)](../reports/output/rapid_assessment_herring_cc.pdf){.btn .btn-primary}\n::::\n\n:::::\n\n\n\n## Management context\n\n\nText in quotation marks is copied exactly as published in DFO's 2024 Sustainability Survey for Fisheries, including any typos.\n\n- **Limit reference point, as described by DFO:** “0.3SBo (unfished spawning biomass) or 14,854 tonnes\\* (estimates are updated annually) \\*value reported from the 2023 stock assessment, implemented for 2023/24 fishery”\n- **Upper stock reference, as described by DFO:** “Implementation of USRs occurred through the 2023/24 Pacific Herring IFMP. For the CC stock, the USR for was set at the average spawning biomass during the productive period (1990-1999). Provisional USRs are considered spawning biomass objectives in the MSE process and are not considered equivalent to the upper control point of the harvest control rule.”\n- **Limit used for this project's indicator:** 0.3 x unfished spawning biomass (SSB0 from the 2018 assessment in RAM)\n- **Management plan, as reported by DFO:** “2023/24 Pacific Herring IFMP - November 7, 2023 - November 6, 2024”\n- **Managed by:** Fisheries and Oceans Canada (DFO)\n\n\n**Science documents cited by DFO in the 2024 survey:**\n\n- <https://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/library-bibliotheque/41231016.pdf>\n\n## Data gaps and caveats\n\n\n- Time series ends in 2018; the DFO zone is from the 2024 survey.\n- No fishing-pressure ratio relative to MSY, so no Kobe plot.\n- Limit reference point taken or derived from RAM Legacy; DFO's current value may differ.\n\n[← Back to all stock cards](../cards.qmd)\n\n",
